      "summary": "President Zelensky on May 2 reported that Ukrainian forces are monitoring unusual military movements on the Belarusian border, accusing Russia of using Belarusian territory to position forces and launch attacks via civilian buildings. Zelensky stated Ukraine is ready to respond and is preparing new sanctions packages, while also anticipating significant diplomatic breakthroughs in May."
    },
    {
      "headline": "Venice Biennale row: Ukraine protests Russia's inclusion; jury resigns, Sybiha calls decision 'cowardly'",
      "summary": "Foreign Minister Sybiha condemned the Venice Biennale's decision to allow Russia to participate in its 2026 exhibition, calling it 'cowardly.' The entire jury subsequently resigned over the matter, which Sybiha framed as demonstrating 'consequences of decisions taken by leading international art platforms.' Italy's culture minister also boycotted. Ukraine also sent an origami deer sculpture to the Biennale as a symbol of resistance."
    },
    {
      "headline": "Defense Minister Fedorov drives drone procurement and air defense scaling; 33,000 drones downed in March",
      "summary": "Defense Minister Mykhailo Fedorov reported that Ukraine shot down a record 33,000 Russian drones in March, and announced procurement of 8,000 Octopus interceptor drones with UK support. He stated Ukraine is targeting 95% drone interception rates, up from 85% in February. Fedorov also signed contracts for mobile F-16 flight simulators and outlined Ukraine's ambition to outpace Russia in technology cycles."
    },
    {
      "headline": "Syrskyi: Ukrainian 'small' air defense downed 2,100 Russian drones in April; Russia running low on air defense missiles",
      "summary": "Commander-in-Chief Syrskyi reported after a meeting on air defense capabilities that Ukraine's small-scale air defense system—comprising interceptor drone units and helicopter crews—destroyed over 2,100 Russian aerial targets in April, with helicopter crews accounting for 500 drones. Syrskyi also stated separately that Russia faces a growing shortage of air defense missiles to counter Ukrainian drones."
    }
  ]
